| Learning/testing/navigation | Instinct/practice/tutorial, Laboratory, shortcuts, accessibility, inspection/credits | W01/W13/W23/W28; isolated state, result wiring, focus, export and lazy resources. Immutable shortcut preparation and borrowed matching remain implemented (SHORTCUT-SNAPSHOT-VERIFY/SHORTCUT-DISPATCH-VERIFY). Ordered conflict caching and retained editor rows are implemented under SHORTCUT-CONFLICT-VERIFY/SHORTCUT-PRESENTATION-VERIFY. Typed configuration-review snapshots and retained publication are implemented under CONFIG-REVIEW-SNAPSHOT-VERIFY/CONFIG-REVIEW-LIFECYCLE-VERIFY; SETTINGS-TEXT-VERIFY covers the shared borrowed-label path. Shared per-event held keys, changed-only logical modifiers and reusable ordered input batches are implemented under KEYBOARD-SNAPSHOT-VERIFY/KEYBOARD-BATCH-VERIFY; event order, fresh host/focus/layout state and quarantine remain required. Narrowed manipulation batches, indexed pointer reconciliation and inactive shortcut capture are implemented under POINTER-BATCH-VERIFY/POINTER-REPLAY-VERIFY/POINTER-CAPTURE-VERIFY. |
| Desktop settings | Overview, gestures, focus policy, width/height presets, keyboard settings, opening rules, external commands, touch/tablet settings | SETTINGS-FIELD-VERIFY, OVERVIEW-GESTURE-VERIFY, WIDTH-DRAFT-VERIFY, WIDTH-SUMMARY-VERIFY and KEYBOARD-SETTINGS-VERIFY cover retained field/view work. SETTINGS-CONTROLS-VERIFY/FOCUS-SETTINGS-VERIFY cover changed-only publication and live policy/status. OPENING-RULE-LIST-VERIFY/OPENING-WINDOW-VERIFY/OPENING-VALIDITY-VERIFY and OPENING-EDITOR-DRAFT-VERIFY/OPENING-EDITOR-OWNER-VERIFY/OPENING-EDITOR-PRESENTATION-VERIFY/OPENING-REFERENCE-VERIFY cover opening rules, editors and reference lifetime. EXTERNAL-DRAFT-VERIFY/EXTERNAL-SETTINGS-VERIFY and ABSOLUTE-DRAFT-VERIFY/ABSOLUTE-PRESENTATION-VERIFY cover retained command/device preparation with live host/request authority. Retain tiny/cold/all-changing cost and memory checks. |
| Shared pointer-hit discovery and drag geometry | native/pointer_hit, hand_camera, shortcuts/editor and layout/desktop/manipulation/pointer | W07/W08/W09/W12/W13/W24; lazy current paint-order hits, query-local camera mapping, current first-target lookup and matched-only published geometry copies are implemented. POINTER-HITS-VERIFY/MANIPULATION-HITS-VERIFY retain clipping/output mapping, blockers/eligibility, duplicate/order semantics and full tiny/all-hit/mixed-camera/drag resource costs. No cross-event hit or authority cache. |
| Store preview and dimension preparation | native/sand_store and sand_store/preview | W01/W08/W12/W13; consumed-only text/default-size preparation and retained exact dimension inputs/output are implemented. STORE-PREVIEW-VERIFY/STORE-DIMENSIONS-VERIFY retain all available Sand kinds, source/IME text, current formatting/repair, layout/glyph behavior and complete opening/quiet/resize costs. Required preview-world construction remains; no shared-world lifecycle change is claimed. |
| Manipulation preparation and preview ownership | native/layout/desktop/manipulation, preparation and previews | Native/application move/resize, nested owners, scaled/spatial/maximized gestures, preview/cancel/commit and concurrent edits; source/map/baseline sharing, first-match comparison and owned membership buffers are implemented. MANIPULATION-SOURCES-VERIFY/MANIPULATION-COMPARISON-VERIFY/MANIPULATION-PREVIEWS-VERIFY retain current authority, source isolation, exact geometry/order and full interaction/resource checks. |
| Desktop controls and automation status | native/layout/desktop/ui/controls and control/presentation; shared input_settings helpers | Toolbar lifecycle, live focus/selection, tiling, effective shortcuts/language and current automation status; ownership/help/status preparation is implemented. DESKTOP-CONTROL-LIFECYCLE-VERIFY/DESKTOP-CONTROL-LABELS-VERIFY/AUTOMATION-STATUS-VERIFY retain exact presentation, recreation, fresh action eligibility and full cost/memory checks. |
| Shared desktop solver | layout/desktop/ordering, rows/solve, scratch and desktop model | W07/W08/W09/W10/W11/W24/W25; stable selected-slot ordering without payload clones, shared visibility, prepared row sizing and selective maximized placement are implemented. LAYOUT-ORDER-VERIFY/LAYOUT-HIDDEN-VERIFY/ROW-SOLVE-VERIFY/MAXIMIZED-PASS-VERIFY retain exact order, bounds, source-state and tiny/large allocation checks; validation and fresh per-invocation solving remain. |
| Desktop focus and dialog placement | native/layout/desktop/focus, focus/memory/restoration and transients/placement | W07/W08/W09/W10/W11/W24/W25; identity-first target lookup, selective saved-focus restoration and requested-ID dialog placement are implemented. FOCUS-TARGET-VERIFY/FOCUS-RESTORATION-VERIFY/TRANSIENT-PLACEMENT-VERIFY cover native/input ownership, deferred retry, first-match/duplicate semantics, original ordered placement and shared normal/preview/transfer behavior; no cross-call target cache or skipped model authoring. |
| Desktop lifecycle and structural checks | native/layout/desktop root scope, preferences, transients/inheritance; shared layout/desktop and rows/validation | W07/W08/W09/W10/W11/W24/W25; root-scoped phase reads, narrow current opening values, indexed restored owners and fresh shared validation facts are implemented. DESKTOP-SCOPE-VERIFY/DESKTOP-PREFERENCES-VERIFY/DESKTOP-INHERITANCE-VERIFY/DESKTOP-VALIDATION-VERIFY cover canonical hierarchy, current ownership, repeated identities, original validation predicates and complete update/resource cost. |
| Desktop resolution and geometry publication | native/layout/desktop, publication, viewport, focus; shared layout/desktop solver | W07/W08/W09/W10/W11/W24/W25; current-phase row/source preparation, retained membership/stamps, inline compact clips, changed-row geometry publication, offset-only reads and mode-specific solver views are implemented. DESKTOP-GEOMETRY-VERIFY/DESKTOP-RESOLVE-VERIFY/DESKTOP-SOLVER-PREPARE-VERIFY cover exact mappings/revisions/order, focus/clip behavior, lifecycle, all layout modes and whole-frame/resource cost. |
| Park/native/client integration | External windows, output/layer-shell controls, launcher, clipboard/drop, capture/lock | W06/W08/W11/W22/W24/W27; independent routing/presentation, lifetime and security epochs. |
| Feature-gated compiled additions | Every extra native/app registration enabled by the actual shipping features, including games where present | Map to existing interaction/media/worker families and a representative start/focus/exit workflow; do not enable optional features solely to inflate the test set. |

Registration alone does not imply a system runs, allocates eagerly or wastes time. For every family, distinguish no instances, visible instances, off-camera instances, inactive workspace, no consumers, active semantic jobs, pending dirty edits and multiple consumers. Record which conditions are applicable rather than pretending every feature supports all of them.
} r_7RD5PQATAM76249CHX70NMXE1S

Park — Finite combination factors (
    @park-dev-9a2b3224933e6e8fa448: 0,
    is #chapter,
    #part-of @park-dev-09-workflows: 81,
    #park-workflow @park-development-cycle
) { r_5JWVNCA294M6734Y1D4K6MABQJ
**Current workflow:** [Development cycle](record:r_043BC6V4K9R3X6E9E4TZP3P6J0). **Resume state:** [Current checkpoint](record:r_2KDK4ZZZJNBEK0J23TFNQAZF9Y).

## Finite combination factors

Use deterministic covering sets over valid pairs of these factors. A factor value does not multiply every underlying feature/Record by every other value. Match each factor pair to a workflow with an actual oracle. The manifest stores included/excluded pairs, scene identity and the reason a combination is inapplicable.

| Factor | Values to represent |
| --- | --- |
| Output activity | One output; two with one quiet; two both active; current mixed output density/scale only where configured. |
| Presentation population | Small/normal/dense; visible/off-camera/inactive; one versus multiple views of same data. |
| Focus/input | Native/client; mouse/touchpad/keyboard/IME; idle/focused editor/composition/pending paste. |
| Navigation/layout | Stationary/pan/zoom/drag/scroll; free/row-column/grid/tiling; nested clip and Fit/Fill; current 2D/3D paths where supported. |
| Data activity | Quiet; local head edit; local body edit; query membership change; remote deterministic update; source/owner replacement. |
| Style activity | Unchanged; local override/reset; inherited/relation change; global switch; continuous slider preview. |
| Background activity | None; required timer/rule; ready query/file task; terminal output; media/shader/video; prepared sync/assistant stream. |
| Storage/worker state | Ready; held/busy; failure then retry; completion after close/replacement; bounded queue pressure. |
| Lifecycle/privacy | First open/reopen; hide/reveal; dirty close/recovery; access revoked; lock/capture policy/output epoch change in existing isolated fixtures. |

Start with the cheap headless/work-count pairs, then run timing for representative normal/dense subsets and hardware-only rendering checks where needed. No compilation/private GPU renderer overlaps a measured physical run. Do not contact real peers, trigger a costly model job, alter real Records or fill the user's canvas to generate this set.
} r_5JWVNCA294M6734Y1D4K6MABQJ

